  "question": {
    "text": "Two metallic spheres of radii $1 \\mathrm{~cm}$ and $3 \\mathrm{~cm}$ are given charges of $-1 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{C}$ and $5 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{C}$, respectively. If these are connected by a conducting wire, the final charge on the bigger sphere is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$2 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{C}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$3 \\times 10^{-2} C$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$4 \\times 10^{-2} C$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1 \\times 10^{-2} C$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\quad \\frac{k x}{1 \\mathrm{~cm}}=\\frac{k(Q-x)}{3 \\mathrm{~cm}}$\n$3 x=Q-x \\Rightarrow 4 x=Q$\n$x=\\frac{Q}{4}=\\frac{4 \\times 10^{-2}}{4} C=1 \\times 10^{-2}$\n$Q^{\\prime}=\\mathrm{Q}-x=3 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{C}$"
  }
}